        "Apiculture and pest control both exploit behaviour, the applied side of {S}. Beekeepers harvest honey by reading colony behaviour and using smoke to trigger honey-storing reflexes; fruit fly traps use pheromone lures that mimic natural communication; stored-grain protection turns on sealing cracks against weevils that follow odour gradients. Managing animals successfully means managing their behaviour and physiology together.",
